From: PinePhone firmware
Subject: [PATCH] flex: a column item's automatic minimum height at its width

In a flex-direction: column container, an item with min-height: auto
had its intrinsic height as its minimum: one that does not depend on
the width, an image's natural height whatever width it is shown at. A
frame holding a 1320 x 757 picture at width: 100% of 432 px was 757
high, the picture in it stretched. The content-based minimum is the
item's height at the width it was just laid out at, when lower.
---
--- a/src/flex_item.cpp
+++ b/src/flex_item.cpp
@@ -414,7 +414,9 @@
                                 el->css().get_height().calc_percent(self_size.height) + el->render_offset_height());
         } else
         {
-            min_size = el->get_intrinsic_min_size().height;
+            // Its content at the width it was laid out at: the intrinsic height does not depend on
+            // the width (an image's is its natural height, at any width)
+            min_size = std::min(el->get_intrinsic_min_size().height, el->height());
         }
     } else
     {
